{
  "title": "Sensei LMS \u2014 edtech (584\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Sensei LMS\nDomain: edtech | Scale: large | Stars: 584\nProblem: Sensei LMS provides educators and knowledge-sharers with a robust, open-source Learning Management System built natively for WordPress, enabling them to create, manage, and deliver online courses, quizzes, and learning experiences without leaving the WordPress ecosystem.\nTarget users: Educators and online course creators, WordPress site owners, E-learning developers and integrators, Training organizations and schools\nCore features: Course creation and management with WordPress block editor support; Quiz and assessment engine; Student enrollment and progress tracking; Analytics and reporting on student and course performance; Learning Mode \u2014 distraction-free, customizable lesson view; Guest/preview access for unregistered users and teacher preview-as-student; MailPoet integration for email communications; WooCommerce integration for selling courses (Sensei Pro)\nIntegrations: WordPress, WooCommerce, MailPoet, VideoPress, WordPress.com managed hosting\nTech stack: React 18, WordPress Block Editor (Gutenberg), SCSS + PHP (WordPress plugin) + MySQL (via WordPress) + WordPress.com / self-hosted WordPress\nKey libraries: @wordpress/block-editor, @wordpress/components, @wordpress/data, @automattic/tour-kit, @automattic/components, lodash, classnames, react, qrcode.react, @playwright/test\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Built as a WordPress plugin monolith, leveraging WordPress hooks and filters extensively to allow third-party extensibility without modifying core code.\n- Frontend is modularized using the Gutenberg block editor paradigm with @wordpress/* packages, enabling a component-driven UI while staying within the WordPress ecosystem.\n- Freemium architecture separates core open-source features (Sensei LMS) from premium capabilities (Sensei Pro), encouraging community adoption while monetizing advanced features.\n- Playwright is used for end-to-end testing alongside a PHP unit test suite, indicating a mature QA strategy across both frontend and backend layers.",
